# SOLID + SWE (apply, don’t recite)

| Principle | Practice |
|-----------|----------|
| **S** | Split UI chrome from domain behavior; one PR concern per cohesive change. |
| **O** | Extend via props/slots/composition; avoid editing closed cores for every variant. |
| **L** | Subtypes must honor the parent contract; no surprise side effects. |
| **I** | Narrow props/APIs; don’t force callers to pass unused baggage. |
| **D** | Depend on stable abstractions (interfaces, hooks, ports) — not concrete fetchers/DB clients deep in UI. |

## SWE non-negotiables
- Correctness > cleverness; readability > novelty.
- Explicit over implicit; immutable data by default where cheap.
- Errors are part of the API: surface, log context, recover or fail.
- Complexity budget: if a change needs a diagram to explain, draw it before merging the idea.
